  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"These three stories, from Bengal, from Orissa to the south, and the Himalayan province of Sikkim to the north, are influenced by local images in their telling. The inset mirror is from Pipli in Orissa where mirrors are ... used in textiles depicting Jagganath. The bird and plant lino-cuts derive from Sikkimese painted wood-carving and the etchings for Miss Sanderson were drawn 'in situ' in Calcutta. The coloured and textured papers were brought from Gangtok, in Sikkim, where they were made by hand"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"The book is printed by letterpress in hand set Plantin. The first copies are on Magnani Velata Avorio hand made paper: the remaining books are on Magnani Aqueforti. Made in London in 2006 in a limited edition of 25 copies"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
